From f44710a38cb8e09569e30da6c4a21ceae1e783b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] XBPython: do not set PYTHONOPTIMIZE on Linux

Kodi sets PYTHONOPTIMIZE=1 before Py_Initialize() on Linux. CPython then
looks exclusively for <mod>.cpython-3X.opt-1.pyc and will not fall back to
the plain .pyc that Debian ships for the standard library and for
dist-packages. Those __pycache__ directories are root-owned while Kodi runs
as the unprivileged 'osmc' user, so the cache CPython wants can never be
written, and importlib swallows the failed write silently (set_data() routes
the EACCES to _bootstrap._verbose_message, which only prints under -v).
Nothing is logged, by Kodi or by Python.

Because every addon invocation runs in a fresh sub-interpreter
(Py_NewInterpreter / Py_EndInterpreter in CPythonInvoker), sys.modules starts
empty each time, so the whole import graph is re-parsed and re-compiled from
source on every single script launch, forever.

Measured on a Vero V (Cortex-A55, bullseye, python3.9): a typical addon
import set of 150 stdlib modules / ~2.9 MiB of source costs ~1520 ms of pure
recompilation per launch, against ~47 ms to unmarshal the equivalent
bytecode - a 37x penalty paid on every launch.

The original justification does not apply here. It was added in 2015 for a
Pi cross-compiled "unified build" sysroot whose .py files had been stripped,
leaving only .pyo. OSMC builds against the system Debian python3 and ships
.py sources alongside Debian's plain .pyc, so the flag buys nothing and
defeats the packaged bytecode cache.

This mirrors the change Dom Cobley made for the Raspberry Pi OS Kodi
packages in 2022, which was never submitted upstream.
See: https://forum.kodi.tv/showthread.php?tid=369573

Signed-off-by: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
---
 xbmc/interfaces/python/XBPython.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/interfaces/python/XBPython.cpp b/xbmc/interfaces/python/XBPython.cpp
index 5fdd17610f..95b1335691 100644
--- a/xbmc/interfaces/python/XBPython.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/interfaces/python/XBPython.cpp
@@ -486,8 +486,10 @@ bool XBPython::OnScriptInitialized(ILanguageInvoker* invoker)
   if (!m_bInitialized)
   {
     // Darwin packs .pyo files, we need PYTHONOPTIMIZE on in order to load them.
-    // linux built with unified builds only packages the pyo files so need it
-#if defined(TARGET_DARWIN) || defined(TARGET_LINUX)
+    // Do not set it on Linux: we link the system python and Debian ships the
+    // stdlib as plain .pyc only, so PYTHONOPTIMIZE would make every import
+    // miss the packaged cache and recompile from source on every script run.
+#if defined(TARGET_DARWIN)
     setenv("PYTHONOPTIMIZE", "1", 1);
 #endif
     // Info about interesting python envvars available
-- 
2.34.1

